- entry .sh   the `sh"…"` interpolator: a `Command` parsed as the code compiles, with escaped substitutions
-     `sh"ls -la $directory"` is a `Command` whose arguments are the words of the literal, split on
-     whitespace with single quotes, double quotes and backslash escapes honoured as a POSIX shell
-     honours them. No shell runs: the arguments go straight to the program, so a metacharacter
-     in a substituted value is never interpreted. The parsing happens while the code compiles,
-     through the `Sh.Runtime` parser, and an error is reported at the character which caused
-     it: _this single quote is never closed_ and _this double quote is never closed_ at the
-     quote that was opened, _a command cannot end with an escape character_ at the trailing
-     backslash, and _an escape character cannot appear immediately before a substitution_ at a
-     backslash written before a `$`.
+ entry .sh   el interpolador `sh"…"`: un `Command` analizado mientras se compila el código, con sustituciones escapadas
+     `sh"ls -la $directory"` es un `Command` cuyos argumentos son las palabras del literal,
+     separadas por los espacios en blanco, respetando las comillas simples, las comillas dobles y
+     los escapes con barra invertida como los respeta una shell POSIX. No se ejecuta ninguna
+     shell: los argumentos van directamente al programa, así que un metacarácter de un valor
+     sustituido nunca se interpreta. El análisis tiene lugar mientras se compila el código,
+     mediante el analizador `Sh.Runtime`, y un error se comunica en el carácter que lo causó:
+     _this single quote is never closed_ y _this double quote is never closed_ en la comilla que
+     se abrió, _a command cannot end with an escape character_ en la barra invertida final, y
+     _an escape character cannot appear immediately before a substitution_ en una barra invertida
+     escrita antes de un `$`.

